WEBVTT

00:00:01.480 --> 00:00:03.710
<i>It is the 25th year of the Taisho Era.</i>

00:00:03.710 --> 00:00:07.920
<i>Ukai Shougo, the son of the current Prime 
Minister of Japan, has come to Fukurou.</i>

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:10.280
<i>As he is the victim of a cursed tome,</i>

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:12.950
<i>the move keeps him far from 
the eyes of the public.</i>

00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:15.640
<i>Shougo had built a wall 
between himself and others,</i>

00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:20.470
<i>but his heart has slowly begun to open,
touched by the girl's pure feelings.</i>

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:24.170
<i>This is the story of Kuze 
Tsugumi and her convictions.</i>

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:28.120
Akatsuki Evening

00:02:25.850 --> 00:02:28.120
-Lilac-

00:02:31.360 --> 00:02:33.630
Another murder?

00:02:36.580 --> 00:02:37.480
Well?

00:02:37.960 --> 00:02:39.570
This is...

00:02:39.570 --> 00:02:41.640
It's a lilac flower.

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:42.740
Hey!

00:02:43.340 --> 00:02:44.620
Who are you?!

00:02:44.620 --> 00:02:45.640
Pardon me.

00:02:45.930 --> 00:02:48.140
I'm Yoshikiri from the 
Imperial Capital Newspaper.

00:02:48.140 --> 00:02:50.640
This area is off limits to
unauthorized personnel!

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:52.220
Little rat, sneaking around here.

00:02:52.220 --> 00:02:54.150
Aw, come on! Just give me a minute!

00:02:56.650 --> 00:02:59.150
<b>Romantic Lilac Night 
Migiwa Shizuru</b>

00:02:56.850 --> 00:02:59.150
Next time, I'll arrest you.

00:02:59.340 --> 00:03:00.440
Honestly...

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:04.660
<b>Imperial Capital University Hospital</b>

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:04.660
Nee-san, I've been waiting for you!

00:03:04.660 --> 00:03:07.040
You look better each time I see you.

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:10.660
The doctor told me your 
burns won't scar too badly.

00:03:11.020 --> 00:03:12.600
More importantly, Nee-san,

00:03:12.600 --> 00:03:16.330
is it true you're living in the same 
building as Migiwa Shizuru-sensei now?

00:03:16.330 --> 00:03:17.670
Well, yes...

00:03:17.670 --> 00:03:19.730
That's awesome! I'm so jealous.

00:03:19.730 --> 00:03:21.510
What do you normally talk about?

00:03:21.510 --> 00:03:23.880
Do you talk about literature and art?

00:03:23.880 --> 00:03:26.430
Do you stay up late having 
passionate discussions?

00:03:26.430 --> 00:03:27.540
Um, well...

00:03:32.980 --> 00:03:34.100
What's wrong?

00:03:34.100 --> 00:03:35.740
Oh, nothing.

00:03:35.740 --> 00:03:39.870
Yes, we talk about literature 
and art... more or less?

00:03:39.870 --> 00:03:40.980
Oh, yeah! Look!

00:03:40.980 --> 00:03:43.950
<b>Romantic Lilac Night
Migiwa Shizuru</b>

00:03:41.560 --> 00:03:44.640
It's Migiwa-sensei's newest 
release, <i>Romantic Lilac Night</i>.

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:46.280
You should read it, too.

00:03:46.740 --> 00:03:50.560
And, well, if at all possible...

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:54.440
get it autographed for me?

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:00.200
<i>I couldn't tell him no.</i>

00:04:01.890 --> 00:04:05.000
<i>"When Yasuhara firmly tugged on Misae's arm,</i>

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:09.550
<i>a charming gasp spilled from her sultry lips.</i>

00:04:09.550 --> 00:04:13.990
<i>Misae still managed to lift her gaze 
and glare sternly at Yasuhara,</i>

00:04:13.990 --> 00:04:18.510
<i>but her heart betrayed her feelings 
as her eyes filled with moisture..."</i>

00:04:22.440 --> 00:04:26.420
<i>It doesn't seem right for Hitaki to 
be reading something like this...</i>

00:04:27.520 --> 00:04:30.020
It's the second incident this week.

00:04:30.500 --> 00:04:31.740
The hallmarks are the same.

00:04:31.740 --> 00:04:35.510
They've gotta be serial murders 
committed by the same killer.

00:04:35.510 --> 00:04:38.140
There was a lilac flower 
in the victim's mouth,

00:04:38.140 --> 00:04:40.030
and a book left at the scene.

00:04:40.300 --> 00:04:42.100
Wait a second, Senpai.

00:04:42.100 --> 00:04:44.040
Was it a cursed tome?

00:04:44.240 --> 00:04:46.550
No, it was a printed book.

00:04:46.550 --> 00:04:50.760
But in a way, this might be an even 
bigger problem than cursed tomes.

00:04:50.970 --> 00:04:52.380
What do you mean?

00:04:52.770 --> 00:04:55.760
<b>Romantic Lilac Night 
Migiwa Shizuru</b>

00:04:53.200 --> 00:04:55.770
This is the book that was left at the scene.

00:04:55.770 --> 00:04:59.090
<b>Romantic Lilac Night 
Migiwa Shizuru</b>

00:04:56.500 --> 00:04:58.180
<i>Romantic Lilac Night</i>?

00:05:09.780 --> 00:05:11.180
Shizuru-san?

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:16.560
Goodness, what an unusual 
place to be selling goldfish.

00:05:16.780 --> 00:05:21.070
Good day, my lovely lady. 
Would you care to purchase one?

00:05:21.410 --> 00:05:24.190
But I've never kept a goldfish before.

00:05:24.190 --> 00:05:28.070
I'm certain these goldfish would 
be happy simply being with

00:05:28.580 --> 00:05:31.060
someone as charming as you.

00:05:31.060 --> 00:05:32.500
My, aren't you smooth?

00:05:32.500 --> 00:05:34.790
In that case, I'll take one.

00:05:36.500 --> 00:05:38.790
Is selling goldfish a side job?

00:05:38.790 --> 00:05:41.080
I would say it's more like I'm helping.

00:05:41.500 --> 00:05:43.600
About a year ago,

00:05:43.600 --> 00:05:46.830
there was an old man who had 
more of them than he could sell.

00:05:46.830 --> 00:05:51.830
I tried selling them to the ladies in the area 
as a test, and they sold out immediately.

00:05:52.660 --> 00:05:56.930
Ever since, I've been helping 
him whenever I have time.

00:05:56.930 --> 00:05:58.920
I think you're well suited to it.

00:05:58.920 --> 00:06:01.370
Don't be so jealous, my princess.

00:06:01.370 --> 00:06:06.130
You're the only one who's truly charming, 
beautiful, and adorable in my eyes.

00:06:06.130 --> 00:06:07.980
I am not jealous.

00:06:09.090 --> 00:06:10.740
Anyway...

00:06:11.020 --> 00:06:14.240
Um... I have a favor to ask of you.

00:06:17.060 --> 00:06:21.320
I told you before that my younger 
brother is a fan of yours, right?

00:06:21.320 --> 00:06:26.260
I was wondering if you might be 
able to sign something for him.

00:06:26.460 --> 00:06:31.460
I'd like to say that I would do 
anything for you, my princess,

00:06:31.460 --> 00:06:35.270
but I don't do autographs. I'm sorry.

00:06:35.270 --> 00:06:38.730
I had no idea. I apologize.

00:06:38.730 --> 00:06:40.560
There's nothing to apologize for.

00:06:42.020 --> 00:06:44.020
How old is your brother?

00:06:44.020 --> 00:06:45.280
He's 14.

00:06:46.460 --> 00:06:48.090
He sounds precocious.

00:06:48.090 --> 00:06:49.730
I can't deny that.

00:06:50.780 --> 00:06:53.920
Well, when you become immersed 
in the world of books,

00:06:53.920 --> 00:06:56.540
your stores of knowledge 
grow, if nothing else.

00:06:57.080 --> 00:07:00.230
However, when that becomes 
the only world you know,

00:07:00.230 --> 00:07:03.290
it may leave you somewhat 
lacking as a person.

00:07:03.740 --> 00:07:05.610
That is true.

00:07:06.120 --> 00:07:09.880
I had the same experience 
when I left my home.

00:07:09.880 --> 00:07:13.160
I realized the world I saw was so... narrow.

00:07:13.660 --> 00:07:17.800
Then perhaps I can help expand your world?

00:07:18.050 --> 00:07:19.860
Please don't tease me!

00:07:22.100 --> 00:07:23.540
We're back.

00:07:24.320 --> 00:07:26.550
There's the man everyone's talking about.

00:07:28.990 --> 00:07:32.620
Are ladies in the city 
spreading rumors about me?

00:07:33.580 --> 00:07:37.190
It's an article about the serial murders 
that have occurred in Ueno Park.

00:07:37.190 --> 00:07:38.740
There have been two victims.

00:07:38.740 --> 00:07:42.440
A lilac flower was stuffed 
in each of their mouths,

00:07:42.440 --> 00:07:45.220
and your book was next to the bodies.

00:07:43.840 --> 00:07:46.320
<b>Another this evening?!</b>

00:07:43.840 --> 00:07:46.320
<b>Tokyo Daily News 
Flowers in the Victims' Mouths 
A Culprit With Bizarre Tastes</b>

00:07:45.220 --> 00:07:46.330
I see.

00:07:46.730 --> 00:07:51.130
This would indeed make me the talk of 
the town among more than just the ladies.

00:07:51.130 --> 00:07:53.840
Do the police suspect Shizuru-san?

00:07:54.090 --> 00:07:58.270
I'd think that Tsubameno guy would 
say something to us first if they did.

00:07:58.270 --> 00:08:02.930
Shizuru-san wouldn't intentionally leave 
his book behind if he were the killer.

00:08:02.930 --> 00:08:05.620
I'm sure the police realize that, too.

00:08:05.620 --> 00:08:08.140
It's more likely that 
someone's trying to ruin

00:08:08.140 --> 00:08:10.780
Shizuru-san's reputation with 
unfounded conspiracy theories.

00:08:12.720 --> 00:08:16.600
Well, you should probably be careful 
what you do for the time being.

00:08:16.950 --> 00:08:19.060
You should probably also cut back on

00:08:19.060 --> 00:08:22.670
flirting and going on dates with 
a different woman every day.

00:08:24.170 --> 00:08:25.780
Were you on a date with Kuze-san today?

00:08:25.780 --> 00:08:26.880
We weren't!

00:08:26.880 --> 00:08:29.620
We just happened to run into 
each other on our way back.

00:08:29.620 --> 00:08:32.700
Oh? I thought of it as a date, though.

00:08:32.700 --> 00:08:33.420
I knew it!

00:08:33.420 --> 00:08:34.770
It wasn't!

00:08:37.120 --> 00:08:38.440
Coming.

00:08:39.350 --> 00:08:42.160
Well, well. I don't often see you at this hour.

00:08:43.930 --> 00:08:45.760
I want to ask you something.

00:08:46.230 --> 00:08:47.260
What is it?

00:08:49.530 --> 00:08:52.900
Do you still have Moritsune 
Saichou's manuscript?

00:08:56.020 --> 00:08:57.910
I did have it before.

00:08:57.910 --> 00:08:59.640
Where is it now?

00:08:59.850 --> 00:09:02.720
You don't need to be so concerned.

00:09:02.720 --> 00:09:04.140
I've already disposed of it.

00:09:05.240 --> 00:09:08.620
That was definitely what 
you all call a cursed tome.

00:09:09.240 --> 00:09:13.410
I could hear the pained voice 
of my teacher coming from it,

00:09:13.780 --> 00:09:16.430
saying, "I'll kill them, I'll kill them."

00:09:18.780 --> 00:09:21.430
So I got scared and burned it.

00:09:22.370 --> 00:09:26.420
His emotional attachment to his work 
was incredibly strong and deep.

00:09:26.880 --> 00:09:30.480
He was always very passionate 
and sincere in his writing.

00:09:31.970 --> 00:09:35.890
His soul must have remained 
in that manuscript.

00:09:35.890 --> 00:09:38.920
Did you really burn it?

00:09:38.920 --> 00:09:40.800
I wouldn't make such a mistake.

00:09:42.300 --> 00:09:43.800
Trust me.

00:09:45.960 --> 00:09:49.440
Ohbayashi Bookstore

00:09:45.960 --> 00:09:49.440
That Ueno Park case sure is scary.

00:09:49.670 --> 00:09:51.670
I hope you solve it quickly.

00:09:51.670 --> 00:09:55.740
If a cursed tome is involved, 
there may be something we can do...

00:09:55.740 --> 00:09:56.820
And you're too close.

00:09:57.260 --> 00:10:00.820
It's speculated that Migiwa 
Shizuru is the real culprit.

00:10:02.330 --> 00:10:04.490
His motive is self-advertisement.

00:10:02.330 --> 00:10:08.830
<b>On Backorder
Migiwa Shizuru's New Release</b>

00:10:04.490 --> 00:10:09.110
In fact, it's been such good advertising 
that his books have been selling very well.

00:10:09.110 --> 00:10:09.600
Listen—

00:10:09.600 --> 00:10:10.330
Let it go.

00:10:13.840 --> 00:10:16.470
<b>Imperial Capital University Hospital</b>

00:10:16.700 --> 00:10:19.470
Nee-san? You don't have to work today?

00:10:19.930 --> 00:10:22.460
I just finished my afternoon patrol.

00:10:23.840 --> 00:10:25.900
Listen, Hitaki...

00:10:26.490 --> 00:10:30.340
It's about Migiwa-sensei, 
right? I believe in him.

00:10:30.340 --> 00:10:34.230
I'm sorry I asked for an autograph 
during such a rough time.

00:10:34.470 --> 00:10:38.460
It's okay. I hope they 
find the killer soon.

00:10:38.460 --> 00:10:39.290
Yeah.

00:10:40.120 --> 00:10:41.260
What's wrong?

00:10:41.750 --> 00:10:45.640
I've read a story about a case 
similar to this before.

00:10:45.640 --> 00:10:48.390
It was a novel by an author 
named Moritsune Saichou.

00:10:48.390 --> 00:10:52.250
Moritsune Saichou... Didn't he 
commit suicide several years ago?

00:10:52.500 --> 00:10:55.940
Yes. He was Migiwa-sensei's teacher.

00:10:55.940 --> 00:11:00.270
But in that story, the flowers being 
stuffed in the corpse's mouths

00:11:00.270 --> 00:11:03.640
were red spider lilies, not lilacs.

00:11:03.640 --> 00:11:07.640
<b>The Purgatory Island Murder Case
Moritsune Saichou</b>

00:11:05.680 --> 00:11:07.650
So you've realized it, too.

00:11:08.540 --> 00:11:09.880
Sasagoi-san.

00:11:09.880 --> 00:11:13.030
<i>The Purgatory Island Murder Case</i>
isn't just a mystery.

00:11:13.260 --> 00:11:16.450
It's the ultimate love story as well as...

00:11:17.960 --> 00:11:21.310
the origin of the murder style imitated 
by the killer in the lilac case

00:11:19.550 --> 00:11:24.290
<b>The Purgatory Island Murder Case
Moritsune Saichou</b>

00:11:21.310 --> 00:11:23.820
that's currently causing such a stir.

00:11:24.990 --> 00:11:26.800
You seem quite well-informed.

00:11:26.800 --> 00:11:29.910
That's because Moritsune-sensei 
was my teacher.

00:11:29.910 --> 00:11:33.040
I've read all his works.

00:11:33.270 --> 00:11:36.630
Moritsune-sensei opened a 
school for novel writing.

00:11:36.630 --> 00:11:39.300
Both Migiwa and I went there.

00:11:39.890 --> 00:11:42.080
He didn't tell you this?

00:11:42.080 --> 00:11:42.800
No.

00:11:43.020 --> 00:11:46.940
I see... Well, I guess it's not something
he'd go out of his way to mention.

00:11:46.940 --> 00:11:52.810
At any rate, he was the first one to 
find Moritsune-sensei after his suicide.

00:11:53.020 --> 00:11:54.390
Shizuru-san did?

00:11:54.390 --> 00:12:00.820
Yes. I wonder if he didn't kill
Moritsune-sensei himself.

00:12:01.240 --> 00:12:03.090
Shizuru-san would never—

00:12:03.090 --> 00:12:06.090
But he had a motive.

00:12:06.740 --> 00:12:08.590
What kind of motive?

00:12:09.640 --> 00:12:14.020
Moritsune-sensei criticized his first book.

00:12:14.020 --> 00:12:16.840
Completely ripped it apart, 
in front of everyone else.

00:12:17.930 --> 00:12:20.440
I bet it was quite mortifying.

00:12:20.440 --> 00:12:23.840
That kind of thing gets 
engraved in your mind.

00:12:24.290 --> 00:12:26.480
He tried to get rid of it, but he couldn't.

00:12:26.480 --> 00:12:32.100
Instead, it just slowly festered, 
until one day he decided to kill him.

00:12:32.340 --> 00:12:34.450
No! Shizuru-san wouldn't—

00:12:34.450 --> 00:12:39.080
But you know, Migiwa has 
Moritsune-sensei's manuscript.

00:12:39.080 --> 00:12:41.020
The final manuscript of a teacher

00:12:41.020 --> 00:12:45.120
he couldn't help but love and respect,
despite hating him enough to want to kill him.

00:12:45.720 --> 00:12:47.870
Are you saying that it's a cursed tome?

00:12:48.090 --> 00:12:51.280
Who knows? I certainly don't.

00:12:51.280 --> 00:12:54.170
But what if Migiwa's been 
reading that manuscript

00:12:54.170 --> 00:12:57.830
all this time, making him 
want to kill someone again?

00:12:57.830 --> 00:12:59.940
Until he actually...

00:13:00.880 --> 00:13:02.250
I'm leaving!

00:13:09.180 --> 00:13:11.010
What are you burning?

00:13:11.600 --> 00:13:14.600
A useless manuscript.

00:13:14.600 --> 00:13:16.520
How dutiful of you.

00:13:16.520 --> 00:13:19.520
It serves as a change of pace, at any rate.

00:13:19.840 --> 00:13:22.130
What are you up to, Nabari-san?

00:13:22.130 --> 00:13:25.270
You're usually holed up in 
your underground laboratory.

00:13:25.760 --> 00:13:30.480
I like to get outside sometimes and breathe
the fresh air, also for a change of pace.

00:13:31.810 --> 00:13:36.780
There's something beautiful and 
fleeting about words becoming flame,

00:13:36.780 --> 00:13:39.040
disappearing into the sky
without being published.

00:13:39.790 --> 00:13:44.280
How poetic of you, Nabari-san. 
You might be cut out to be a writer.

00:13:44.570 --> 00:13:47.280
Not at all. That isn't for me.

00:13:47.710 --> 00:13:49.770
Well, I'll be heading back.

00:13:49.770 --> 00:13:51.570
Yes, see you later.

00:14:00.840 --> 00:14:04.370
Murderer!

00:14:11.490 --> 00:14:12.630
There was a witness?

00:14:12.630 --> 00:14:16.340
According to eyewitness testimony 
from the third incident last night,

00:14:16.340 --> 00:14:18.620
the killer was holding 
a Japanese-style book.

00:14:18.620 --> 00:14:19.760
Which means...

00:14:19.760 --> 00:14:22.480
Fukurou can now investigate this case, too.

00:14:28.940 --> 00:14:30.770
Ukai, where's Shizuru-san?

00:14:30.770 --> 00:14:34.760
How would I know? I'm not his butler.

00:14:35.040 --> 00:14:39.270
You may not be his butler, but neither 
of you are typical housemates, right?

00:14:39.270 --> 00:14:43.140
Don't lump me in with that freak! 
How extremely unpleasant!

00:14:48.520 --> 00:14:56.370
Cute little goldfish all dressed in red...

00:14:53.010 --> 00:14:54.320
Shizuru-san?

00:14:57.980 --> 00:14:59.830
I'm on my way back from selling goldfish.

00:14:59.830 --> 00:15:02.410
You shouldn't be going out so much right now.

00:15:02.410 --> 00:15:04.390
Are you worried about me?

00:15:04.390 --> 00:15:05.300
Of course I am.

00:15:06.980 --> 00:15:08.300
Do you think...

00:15:08.630 --> 00:15:09.500
What?

00:15:11.030 --> 00:15:12.800
that I'm the killer?

00:15:14.870 --> 00:15:18.910
I don't... I don't think that at all!

00:15:21.170 --> 00:15:22.310
We have trouble!

00:15:22.590 --> 00:15:24.850
What're you in such a panic for?

00:15:25.980 --> 00:15:29.000
Migiwa-sensei is being taken 
in as a material witness!

00:15:31.650 --> 00:15:34.040
Would you accompany us to the station?

00:15:35.000 --> 00:15:36.810
What is this all about?

00:15:36.810 --> 00:15:40.830
Your book, <i>Romantic Lilac Night</i>, 
is always left at the crime scenes.

00:15:41.550 --> 00:15:43.200
And then there's this book.

00:15:42.830 --> 00:15:48.840
<b>Purgatory Island Murder Case
Moritsune Saichou</b>

00:15:43.760 --> 00:15:46.570
Since you were a student 
of Moritsune Saichou,

00:15:46.570 --> 00:15:48.840
we would very much like to talk to you.

00:15:49.500 --> 00:15:53.340
I swear, it's because of books like this 
that these crimes are happening.

00:15:53.580 --> 00:15:54.930
The book is not to blame!

00:15:54.930 --> 00:15:55.850
Who are you?

00:15:56.360 --> 00:15:59.990
She is correct. The book is not to blame.

00:15:59.990 --> 00:16:03.440
A human is at fault here for trying 
to bring fiction into reality.

00:16:03.440 --> 00:16:07.340
Then will you tell us about 
this human who is at fault?

00:16:07.340 --> 00:16:09.860
We can take our time in 
the interrogation room.

00:16:14.080 --> 00:16:15.370
Shizuru-san!

00:16:16.430 --> 00:16:17.870
There's nothing to worry about.

00:16:18.320 --> 00:16:21.870
We will catch the killer for sure!

00:16:22.140 --> 00:16:26.310
Thank you, but you shouldn't get 
too deeply involved, my princess.

00:16:26.310 --> 00:16:27.200
Get moving!

00:16:27.200 --> 00:16:27.880
Okay, okay.

00:16:35.130 --> 00:16:35.890
Listen up.

00:16:36.170 --> 00:16:39.390
All the incidents have been 
occurring near Ueno Park.

00:16:39.880 --> 00:16:42.870
We will be investigating in 
the vicinity tonight, as well.

00:16:45.580 --> 00:16:49.730
Will the killer even show up
with such tight security?

00:16:51.730 --> 00:16:53.920
Let me know right away if you see any auras,

00:16:53.920 --> 00:16:55.770
and I'll signal Akira and the others.

00:16:56.250 --> 00:16:56.910
Okay.

00:17:04.080 --> 00:17:06.480
I have nothing more to tell you.

00:17:06.480 --> 00:17:08.300
May I go home now?

00:17:08.300 --> 00:17:09.520
Can't do that.

00:17:09.520 --> 00:17:11.900
We've found that the victim 
from the third incident

00:17:11.900 --> 00:17:14.660
that occurred last night 
bought a goldfish from you.

00:17:16.340 --> 00:17:20.560
The victims from the two previous 
incidents are familiar with you, as well.

00:17:20.560 --> 00:17:22.880
One is an employee at a café you frequent,

00:17:22.880 --> 00:17:26.310
and the other is a woman you had 
drinks with at a dance hall.

00:17:26.580 --> 00:17:29.120
Why them?

00:17:29.120 --> 00:17:30.800
That's what we're asking!

00:17:33.590 --> 00:17:38.300
What's <i>The Purgatory Island 
Murder Case</i> about, anyway?

00:17:38.800 --> 00:17:42.060
Aggravated by a twisted 
love for the protagonist,

00:17:42.060 --> 00:17:45.810
the culprit kills the women involved with 
the protagonist one after the other.

00:17:48.440 --> 00:17:51.560
Some people say it's the 
ultimate love story,

00:17:52.400 --> 00:17:54.830
but it's a story of twisted love.

00:17:54.830 --> 00:17:58.670
In the end, the culprit kills the person 
the protagonist loves the most,

00:17:58.670 --> 00:18:02.740
and blinded by hatred from losing
their beloved, the protagonist

00:18:02.740 --> 00:18:04.100
then kills the culprit.

00:18:04.750 --> 00:18:10.560
It's a story of the culprit's ultimate 
goal to be killed by the one they love.

00:18:11.360 --> 00:18:13.050
I get it.

00:18:13.050 --> 00:18:16.850
Love's opposite extreme 
isn't hate; it's apathy.

00:18:17.270 --> 00:18:20.590
The culprit would take
feeling hated over apathy,

00:18:20.590 --> 00:18:24.220
and so they longed to be killed.

00:18:25.240 --> 00:18:28.120
Might I be allowed to use the bathroom?

00:18:28.480 --> 00:18:30.630
Tsubameno, you go with him.

00:18:31.330 --> 00:18:32.120
Yes, sir.

00:18:33.840 --> 00:18:37.130
I'm sorry it's turned out like this.

00:18:37.370 --> 00:18:40.390
I don't mind. By the way, Tsubameno-kun...

00:18:40.390 --> 00:18:41.380
What is it?

00:18:41.630 --> 00:18:44.080
May I ask a favor of you?

00:18:48.860 --> 00:18:50.010
An aura!

00:18:55.590 --> 00:18:56.240
Akira!

00:18:56.240 --> 00:18:57.110
After him!

00:18:59.220 --> 00:19:00.030
Crap!

00:19:00.440 --> 00:19:02.620
The culprit is heading toward Ueno Park.

00:19:02.620 --> 00:19:04.270
Kuze, you wait here!

00:19:14.880 --> 00:19:16.030
A lilac?

00:19:16.780 --> 00:19:20.780
<b>Bathroom</b>

00:19:18.030 --> 00:19:19.220
Hey, Tsubameno!

00:19:19.220 --> 00:19:20.280
What happened?

00:19:21.180 --> 00:19:24.400
The material witness has escaped!

00:19:32.090 --> 00:19:36.060
I was just asked to burn 
this book in Ueno Park!

00:19:36.810 --> 00:19:37.800
What?

00:19:50.810 --> 00:19:51.950
Hayato!

00:19:51.950 --> 00:19:53.210
That was close.

00:20:02.820 --> 00:20:07.820
The culprit in Moritsune-sensei's novel 
wouldn't use such a vulgar weapon.

00:20:08.040 --> 00:20:09.320
Shizuru-san!

00:20:09.320 --> 00:20:11.260
Sorry I'm a bit late.

00:20:13.620 --> 00:20:15.380
Migiwa-sensei!

00:20:15.380 --> 00:20:16.830
Migiwa-sensei...

00:20:17.080 --> 00:20:21.840
Ah, Migiwa-sensei, it's me. 
I finally got to meet you!

00:20:22.140 --> 00:20:25.840
I don't know the likes of you.

00:20:26.110 --> 00:20:30.750
Yes, though I love you so much,
you don't even know I exist.

00:20:30.750 --> 00:20:36.460
That's why I destroyed them all! 
All those you hold most dear!

00:20:36.460 --> 00:20:40.630
Those eyes... They look 
at me full of such hatred.

00:20:40.860 --> 00:20:45.660
Now, from this moment on, 
my existence will be deeply... deeply...

00:20:45.660 --> 00:20:47.810
deeply engraved in your soul!

00:20:47.810 --> 00:20:50.140
Like a wound that will never heal!

00:20:50.400 --> 00:20:53.690
Now, please give me all 
your feelings of hatred!

00:20:53.690 --> 00:20:56.010
Hurry! Hurry and kill me, please!

00:20:56.010 --> 00:20:58.760
With your own hands!

00:20:58.760 --> 00:21:01.230
There is a difference between 
fiction and reality.

00:21:01.230 --> 00:21:03.890
I cannot grant your wish.

00:21:08.620 --> 00:21:10.420
Come on, keep walking.

00:21:14.640 --> 00:21:17.190
People will atone for their sins.

00:21:17.190 --> 00:21:20.380
It's just like you said. 
The book is not to blame.

00:21:21.830 --> 00:21:22.670
Yeah.

00:21:24.420 --> 00:21:27.050
<b>Romantic Lilac Night
Migiwa Shizuru</b>

00:21:25.080 --> 00:21:27.030
It's Migiwa-sensei's autograph!

00:21:27.500 --> 00:21:29.680
He said he'd make a special 
exception for you.

00:21:29.680 --> 00:21:32.220
Migiwa-sensei is so nice, isn't he?

00:21:32.220 --> 00:21:34.540
I bet you're his fan now, too.

00:21:35.030 --> 00:21:38.080
Yes, my perspective of him 
might have changed a bit.

00:21:42.280 --> 00:21:45.250
In the end, I'm no different 
from that killer.

00:21:45.960 --> 00:21:49.000
I may have been captivated 
by Sensei's manuscript.

00:23:20.460 --> 00:23:22.500
<i>Hiya! This is Perry, kyu!</i>

00:23:21.210 --> 00:23:36.430
Chapter 6:  "Mother's Face -Kingfisher-"

00:23:22.500 --> 00:23:24.710
<i>Thank you for always playing with me, kyu.</i>

00:23:24.710 --> 00:23:27.840
<i>Perry loves you too, kyu!</i>

00:23:27.840 --> 00:23:30.010
<i>Pet me some more, kyu-kyu.</i>

00:23:30.010 --> 00:23:32.890
<i>Speaking of, Kuina said something 
about missing out on a bargain, kyu.</i>

00:23:32.890 --> 00:23:34.890
<i>Apparently it was a crushing defeat, kyu.</i>

00:23:34.890 --> 00:23:37.850
<i>Well, I'll be waiting for you at 
the shop, kyu-kyu-kyu-kyun!</i>
